  "prefLabel": "Pes 1002.03 Division Investigation",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Pes 1002.03 Division Investigation. Investigation of a potential site management area by the division for purposes of obtaining information shall be initiated based on the detection of a pesticide in at least 2 samples taken at different times from a groundwater or surface water sampling point. However, an area where pesticide use has resulted in contamination which violates state ambient groundwater quality standards shall not be designated a site management area and shall be regulated under RSA 485:3 and Env-Wm 1403.\n\nSource. #5702, eff 9-17-93; ss by #6316, eff 8-13-96; ss by #8131, eff 8-13-04; ss by #10333, eff 5-10-13; ss by #14064, eff 8-22-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/pes1000.html"
